//! Golden test of every vanilla `minecraft:jigsaw` structure (villages, pillager outpost, bastion remnant, ancient city, trail
//! ruins, trial chambers incl. its pool aliases, abandoned camps) against the real vanilla classes (fixture
//! `tests/fixtures/jigsaw_structures.txt.gz`, generated by `tests/oracle/JigsawStructureOracle.java`): the generated start (every
//! piece's saved tag: pool element, junctions, rotation, ground level delta, bounding box, ...) for several seeds/chunks, the
//! `Beardifier` built from the start for the chunks around it (affected box + sampled values), and `placeInChunk` of the start
//! (reloaded from its own saved tag, like a persisted chunk) over synthetic terrain: blocks as a per-chunk digest, block entity
//! NBT (loot chests, spawners, ...), scheduled ticks, heightmaps, post-processing marks, region random.

